[0.472, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 18 \u001b[22m 2026-11-15 baseline, and the lines it cites no longer exist. Manifest's side of these checks\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m1\u001b[11G\u001b[22marriv\u001b[17Gs with H06 and late\u001b[37G stages.\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m2\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 21 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m**Status, 2026-11-23:** the space extraction                                                           \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 22 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mJettison's plan\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](../../jettison/docs/space-extraction-plan.md)) is done. The engine keeps only       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 23 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mwhat has a neutral name and serves more than one genre; the space setting, star systems, their         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 24 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242morbits and the galaxy, cruising, jump lanes, gates and routes, is Manifest's `space` module            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 25 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116marchitecture\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](architecture.md#space)), which tests all space code, and the engine's space sample     \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 26 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mis retired. Jettison's `neutral_words` suite holds its modules to none of the setting's words.         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 27 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mEvery Manifest suite and pinned hash held on the local engine at Jettison `359ad42`.                   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 28 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                           