[0.154, "o", "\u001b[H\r\u001b[46C\u001b[8B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m Jump to bottom (ctrl+End) ↓ \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m/btw \u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153msince all the save games are just test data and they are all in manifest or jettison and can be rewritten, c…\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BYes, that's a reasonable ca\u001b[33Gl\u001b[36Gand it's yo\u001b[48Grs\u001b[51Gto make. Nothing outside the two\u001b[84Grepos holds\u001b[96Ga \u001b[99Gave or a\u001b[108Gdefinition\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bfile, so a migration here protects only test data you can rewrite. But it is a change of policy, not a cleanup,\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Band a few things come with it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat it would mean\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B- \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdocs/architecture.md\u001b[39m (\"Persiste\u001b[39Gce\") says th\u001b[52Gt what a\u001b[61Gbuild\u001b[67Gwrote,\u001b[74Gevery\u001b[80Glater\u001b[86Gbuild\u001b[92Gloads.\u001b[99GIt\u001b[102Galso\u001b[107Gsays\u001b[112Gthe\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B fixtu\u001b[14Gs (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mworld-v1.save\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mworld-v2.save\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249msave-v1.save\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mreplay-layout3.save\u001b[39m, and th\u001b[89G dock's\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mharbour-version-4.world\u001b[39m from\u001b[36Gslice 7) are \"never regenerated\". That rul\u001b[79G would change\u001b[93Gto \u001b[97Gomething like\u001b[111G\"until\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1Bplayers\u001b[15Gkeep\u001b[20Gsaves,\u001b[27Ga\u001b[29Gformat\u001b[36Gchange\u001b[43Grewrites the fixtures instead of migrating\".\u001b[88GIt\u001b[91Gneeds\u001b[97Gwriting\u001b[105Gdown\u001b[110Gin\u001b[113Gthe\r\u001b[1B      docs and in \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdecisions.md\u001b[39m, or a later review will flag the missing migrations again.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  - Your earlier instruction for slice 7 was \"a save written before loads\". Dropping migrations reverses that, so it\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1Bshould\u001b[14Gbe\u001b[17Grecorded\u001b[26Gas\u001b[29Gyour\u001b[34Gdecision\u001b[43Gwith\u001b[48Ga\u001b[50Gdate.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[3m↑/↓\u001b[10Gscroll · c to copy · f to fork · Esc to close\u001b[23m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H"]
