mping\u001b[108Gmeans\u001b[114Gno\u001b[117Gpin\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gmoves from versioning. A pin moves only when the bytes really \u001b[69Ghange, and i\u001b[82G re-pinned\u001b[93Gwith \u001b[99Ghe usual\u001b[108Gproof\u001b[114Gthat\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bonly bytes\u001b[17Gchanged, not state.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mStale data fails loudly instead of being misread.\u001b[56G\u001b[22mThe\u001b[60Greaders\u001b[68Galready\u001b[76Grefuse\u001b[83Gan\u001b[86Gunknown\u001b[94Gfield\u001b[100Gby\u001b[103Gname\u001b[108Gand\u001b[112Gline,\u001b[118Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Ga foreign version by name. One new rule closes the r\u001b[59Gmaining g\u001b[69Gp: if a field's meaning or type chang\u001b[107Gs, it gets\u001b[119G\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bnew name,\u001b[16Gso an old file is r\u001b[36Gfused rathe\u001b[82G keeps \u001b[90Gts\u001b[93Gdefault, which is harmless.\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
