[0.170, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mme and serves more than one genre; the space setting moves into Manifest, which tests all space code; \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe space sample is retired; jump lanes and gates stay as portals for Manifest's stargates; neutral mo\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mdules use none of the setting's words; every Manifest pin holds. **Done** 2026-11-23, in eight slices \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[5G \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mthe plan\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](space-extraction-plan.md)): the vocabulary check (`neutral_words`); the sample, Jetsam, `s\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m \u001b[5G \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mpacescene` and the cargo deck retired, render_test the shell with no game over static scenes; the spac\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242me-only reasons, the scene's star system and the save's migration in neutral words; `transit` (motion p\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mrofiles, passages, portals, slots, gated portals) with consumers of no genre, the cruise, lanes and ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[5G \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtes rebuilt on it with no pin moved; the docks' platforms, berths and vehicles; `celestial` and `space\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m` moved into Manifest's `space`; the saved names renamed, pins moved once by the names alone; and the \r\u001b